Author: Kanban Agent <agent@kanban.local>
Date:   Sat Nov 21 14:22:24 2026 -0500

    feat(attachments): allow application/pdf with bounded subprocess active-content rejection (KAN-81)
    
    - Scaffold migration p6_02_pdf_attachments widening attachments_content_type_check to include application/pdf and adding nullable page_count column.
    - Implement zero-new-dependency stdlib zlib PDF structural scanner in kanban/attachments/pdf.py with bounded child subprocess (timeout <= 3.0s, 512 MiB memory cap).
    - Enforce Flate decompression bomb defenses (<=100x ratio, <=50 MiB stream, <=100 MiB total, <=50,000 objects), #XX hex name normalization, and /ObjStm object stream scanning.
    - Reject forbidden active content keys (/JS, /JavaScript, /AA, /OpenAction, /Launch, /EmbeddedFiles, /RichMedia, /XFA, /GoToR, /SubmitForm, /ImportData, /Encrypt, non-https /URI) with HTTP 422 UNSAFE_PDF_CONTENT.
    - Enforce forced-download security headers on /api/v1/attachments direct and signed URL retrieval routes (Content-Disposition: attachment; filename="<safe>.pdf", Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; sandbox, X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff).
    - Implement frontend PdfAttachmentCard with document icon, byte size, verified page count, truncated SHA-256 badge, and safe download action.
    - Update SafeMarkdownPreview to resolve attachment:// links into PdfAttachmentCard, fix premature placeholder insertion in CommentComposer, and populate split-section-attachments in IssueSurface.
    - Document Architecture Decision Record in docs/adr/ADR-PDF-HANDLING.md and compile forensic proof packet in docs/qa/KAN-81/.

